n-views.md` states the `fact-signer` case. `operate-a-service.md` links \"Bind a new room to GitHub\" on `self-host-mac.md`. `write-an-application.md` says the first guard of `say` requires `counting` and the other three name reasons.\n- The checks. On my own extracted copy of the head, `scripts/check-doc-links.mjs` checks 1,175 local links and finds none broken. `security-witnesses.mjs` reports 13 witnesses, 5 invariants and 9 files. `security-settings.mjs` and `security-entry-points.mjs` exit 0. `scripts/check-notes.mjs 6bfb6e16 8631e209` reports 0 warnings.\n\nWhat holds:\n\n- Scope. Main 6bfb6e16 is an ancestor, the head is pushed, and the planner's worktree is clean at the head. Against main, the head adds or changes exactly the 22 paths that its 22 artifacts cover, all Markdown, and deletes `apps/room/docs/ledger.md` by the rename. The commit-message check passes: 1 checked, 0 flagged.\n\nArchitecture: sound. Reader pages now state what is true and how to do it, and the history of who decided and what ran lives in notes that keep it word for word.\n\nSecurity: no finding. Each security rule keeps its qualification. The change drops attribution, not limits, and it adds no credential, route or setting.\n\nSimplification: no required change.\n\nNo setting changes. This approval authorizes no deployment or publication.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:07431149663f749749b4cde84b0b44f3c40d640b","binding":"assigned","head":"8631e20989220beaa47b3a4ae78db639e2b6fd5a","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:c8c99d263b5d5c25a02b40d49c5d51f6540024e2\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:c11d7b7451f231d59f253174f2595bcce850f2fd\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:669af156705ccaa8e5b6f5f93227173d8b89ca70","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}